From: Ben <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:33:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] napari_trainer: train on a per-run copy of the config and
 the paired layers

run_training changed the GUI's selected config in place: its data_path,
targets, patch size and ops. A later run or a weights-only inference
fallback then saw the last run's settings instead of the selected YAML
(ink -> surface -> ink lost ignore_label: 2). Each run now works on a
deep copy of the selected config.

The layer export paired a label with every image whose name it starts
with ('vol_crop_ink' also matched 'vol'), accepted labels of another
shape or on another grid (sampled at the image's raw indices), wrote to
paths built from layer display names with overwrite on, and left the
export behind. A config with dataset_config.volumes or a cross_frame
dataset read its own data instead. Now a label belongs to the image with
the longest matching name, it must have the image's shape, scale,
translate, rotate, shear and affine, targets must be plain names, such
configs are rejected, and the export is written under indexed names to
a per-run temporary directory that is removed when the run ends, also
after an error. The optional <image>_mask layer is still not used.

The Min Labeled Percentage had no effect: without a patch cache
ZarrDataset enumerates every patch. The run now writes the cache with
vesuvius.find_patches' generator (split so it takes a loaded config),
selecting patches by the widget's percentage (bounding-box criterion
off), and stops with an error when no patch qualifies. 3D layers with
Patch Size Z 0 stop with an error instead of reaching the 2D sampler.

Only nnUNet_DC_and_CE_loss is offered: the BCE losses fail on the
default two-channel prediction and one-channel target, MSE/L1 broadcast
the label over both channels, and the standalone Dice loss does not
honour the ignore label.

