From cbea85f479e8373913ef80768500f7a47cdba441 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:33:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] napari_trainer: restore the checkpoint's network and stop
 on missing weights

Building from the checkpoint config missed three layouts the GUI config
path had loaded: a target on the shared decoder next to one with its own
decoder (the saved config says separate_decoders: true globally, so the
shared target got a new, untrained decoder), the nested legacy 'config'
(read as if it were the model config), and Primus, which saves its patch
as input_shape while inference tiles with patch_size. Each target now
gets the decoder its weights were saved with, the legacy config is
unwrapped as vesuvius.predict does, and input_shape is returned as
patch_size.

load_state_dict(strict=False) also printed success when network tensors
were missing from the checkpoint, and the output layer came from
untrained weights. Missing tensors (and shape mismatches) now stop
inference with an error before any layer is added; extra checkpoint
tensors, such as deep-supervision or old shared-decoder heads, are
skipped as before. DDP/torch.compile key prefixes are stripped.

